<#
.SYNOPSIS
    DORA Evidence Collection — orchestrator. Runs all nine evidence-gathering
    scripts in this set and merges their output into one master CSV.

.DESCRIPTION
    This script does NOT gather evidence itself. It calls the nine individual
    DORA-Evidence-*.ps1 scripts in this folder, one after another, and then
    combines every CSV they produce into a single DORA-Evidence-MASTER.csv,
    sorted by DORA Article and Section, with a SourceScript column added so you
    can trace every row back to where it came from.

    It does NOT answer Yes/Partly/No for you, and it does NOT write anything
    back into the DORA Self-Assessment workbook. See
    "DORA-Evidence-Scripts-README.md" in this folder for the full explanation
    of what these scripts are, what they check, and how to use the output.

    WHY A SEPARATE ORCHESTRATOR AND NOT ONE BIG SCRIPT: each of the nine scripts
    is independently runnable and independently documented, with its own
    .SYNOPSIS/.DESCRIPTION/.NOTES explaining exactly what it checks and what its
    blind spots are. Keeping them separate means you can run just the one you
    need (e.g. only the backup check) without pulling in Graph AND Azure AND
    Security module dependencies every time.

.PARAMETER OutputFolder
    Where to write all CSV output (individual reports + the merged master
    report). Created automatically if it doesn't exist. Defaults to
    ".\DORA-Evidence-Output" under the current directory.

.PARAMETER SubscriptionId
    Passed through to every Azure Resource Manager-based script (backup,
    logging, patching, asset inventory, encryption, network, secure score).
    If omitted, each script uses whatever subscription your current Azure
    context defaults to — check with Get-AzContext beforehand if you're not
    sure which one that is.

.PARAMETER Exclude
    Friendly names of scripts to SKIP this run. Valid values: ConditionalAccess,
    BackupRecovery, PrivilegedAccess, LoggingMonitoring, PatchManagement,
    AssetInventory, Encryption, NetworkSegmentation, SecureScore.
    Example: -Exclude PatchManagement,SecureScore

.PARAMETER SkipAzurePolicyCheck
    Passed through to the Conditional Access script to skip its optional
    Part 2 (Azure Policy DORA initiative lookup), which requires a second,
    separate Azure sign-in on top of the Graph sign-in.

.EXAMPLE
    .\Run-DORAEvidenceCollection.ps1

    Runs all nine scripts against your default Graph tenant and default Azure
    subscription, writes output to .\DORA-Evidence-Output\

.EXAMPLE
    .\Run-DORAEvidenceCollection.ps1 -SubscriptionId "11111111-2222-3333-4444-555555555555" -Exclude PatchManagement

    Runs everything except the patch management check, against a specific
    subscription.

.NOTES
    You will be prompted to sign in more than once — Microsoft Graph and Azure
    Resource Manager are separate authentication contexts, and PowerShell does
    not automatically share a session between Connect-MgGraph and
    Connect-AzAccount. In practice you'll typically see one Graph sign-in
    prompt (reused across the Graph-based scripts) and one Azure sign-in
    prompt (reused across the Azure Resource Manager-based scripts), not nine
    separate prompts — but don't be alarmed if it asks twice.
#>

[CmdletBinding()]
param(
    [string]$OutputFolder = ".\DORA-Evidence-Output",
    [string]$SubscriptionId,
    [ValidateSet("ConditionalAccess","BackupRecovery","PrivilegedAccess","LoggingMonitoring",
                 "PatchManagement","AssetInventory","Encryption","NetworkSegmentation","SecureScore")]
    [string[]]$Exclude = @(),
    [switch]$SkipAzurePolicyCheck
)

$ErrorActionPreference = "Continue"
$scriptDir = Split-Path -Parent $MyInvocation.MyCommand.Path

if (-not (Test-Path $OutputFolder)) {
    New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path $OutputFolder | Out-Null
}
$OutputFolder = (Resolve-Path $OutputFolder).Path

Write-Host ""
Write-Host "======================================================================" -ForegroundColor Magenta
Write-Host " DORA Evidence Collection — running all evidence-gathering scripts" -ForegroundColor Magenta
Write-Host " Output folder: $OutputFolder" -ForegroundColor Magenta
Write-Host "======================================================================" -ForegroundColor Magenta
Write-Host ""

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Registry of all nine scripts: friendly name, filename, output CSV name,
# and the extra parameters (if any) each one needs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
$scriptRegistry = @(
    @{ Name = "ConditionalAccess";   File = "DORA-Evidence-ConditionalAccess.ps1";   Output = "DORA-Evidence-Report.csv";              ExtraParams = @{ SkipAzurePolicyCheck = $SkipAzurePolicyCheck } }
    @{ Name = "BackupRecovery";      File = "DORA-Evidence-BackupRecovery.ps1";      Output = "DORA-Evidence-BackupRecovery.csv";      ExtraParams = @{} }
    @{ Name = "PrivilegedAccess";    File = "DORA-Evidence-PrivilegedAccess.ps1";    Output = "DORA-Evidence-PrivilegedAccess.csv";    ExtraParams = @{} }
    @{ Name = "LoggingMonitoring";   File = "DORA-Evidence-LoggingMonitoring.ps1";   Output = "DORA-Evidence-LoggingMonitoring.csv";   ExtraParams = @{} }
    @{ Name = "PatchManagement";     File = "DORA-Evidence-PatchManagement.ps1";     Output = "DORA-Evidence-PatchManagement.csv";     ExtraParams = @{} }
    @{ Name = "AssetInventory";      File = "DORA-Evidence-AssetInventory.ps1";      Output = "DORA-Evidence-AssetInventory.csv";      ExtraParams = @{} }
    @{ Name = "Encryption";          File = "DORA-Evidence-Encryption.ps1";          Output = "DORA-Evidence-Encryption.csv";          ExtraParams = @{} }
    @{ Name = "NetworkSegmentation"; File = "DORA-Evidence-NetworkSegmentation.ps1"; Output = "DORA-Evidence-NetworkSegmentation.csv"; ExtraParams = @{} }
    @{ Name = "SecureScore";         File = "DORA-Evidence-SecureScore.ps1";         Output = "DORA-Evidence-SecureScore.csv";         ExtraParams = @{} }
)

$runLog = [System.Collections.Generic.List[PSCustomObject]]::new()

foreach ($entry in $scriptRegistry) {

    if ($Exclude -contains $entry.Name) {
        Write-Host "[SKIPPED] $($entry.Name) (excluded)" -ForegroundColor DarkGray
        $runLog.Add([PSCustomObject]@{ Script = $entry.Name; Result = "Skipped (excluded)" })
        continue
    }

    $scriptPath = Join-Path $scriptDir $entry.File
    if (-not (Test-Path $scriptPath)) {
        Write-Warning "[NOT FOUND] $($entry.File) — expected at $scriptPath. Skipping."
        $runLog.Add([PSCustomObject]@{ Script = $entry.Name; Result = "Not found" })
        continue
    }

    $outputPath = Join-Path $OutputFolder $entry.Output

    Write-Host ""
    Write-Host "----------------------------------------------------------------------" -ForegroundColor Cyan
    Write-Host " Running: $($entry.Name)  ($($entry.File))" -ForegroundColor Cyan
    Write-Host "----------------------------------------------------------------------" -ForegroundColor Cyan

    $params = @{ OutputPath = $outputPath }
    if ($SubscriptionId -and $entry.Name -ne "ConditionalAccess" -and $entry.Name -ne "PrivilegedAccess") {
        # Conditional Access and Privileged Access are Graph/tenant-scoped, not subscription-scoped
        $params["SubscriptionId"] = $SubscriptionId
    }
    foreach ($key in $entry.ExtraParams.Keys) {
        if ($entry.ExtraParams[$key]) { $params[$key] = $entry.ExtraParams[$key] }
    }

    try {
        & $scriptPath @params
        if (Test-Path $outputPath) {
            $runLog.Add([PSCustomObject]@{ Script = $entry.Name; Result = "Completed" })
        } else {
            $runLog.Add([PSCustomObject]@{ Script = $entry.Name; Result = "Ran, but no output file produced — check console output above for errors" })
        }
    } catch {
        Write-Warning "[FAILED] $($entry.Name): $($_.Exception.Message)"
        $runLog.Add([PSCustomObject]@{ Script = $entry.Name; Result = "Failed: $($_.Exception.Message)" })
    }
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Merge every CSV produced into one master report
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Write-Host ""
Write-Host "======================================================================" -ForegroundColor Magenta
Write-Host " Merging individual reports into DORA-Evidence-MASTER.csv" -ForegroundColor Magenta
Write-Host "======================================================================" -ForegroundColor Magenta

$allRows = [System.Collections.Generic.List[PSCustomObject]]::new()

foreach ($entry in $scriptRegistry) {
    $outputPath = Join-Path $OutputFolder $entry.Output
    if (-not (Test-Path $outputPath)) { continue }

    $rows = Import-Csv -Path $outputPath
    foreach ($row in $rows) {
        $row | Add-Member -NotePropertyName "SourceScript" -NotePropertyValue $entry.Name -Force
        $allRows.Add($row)
    }
}

if ($allRows.Count -eq 0) {
    Write-Warning "No evidence rows were collected. Check the run log below and the console output above for errors."
} else {
    $sorted = $allRows | Sort-Object { [int]$_.Article }, Section
    $masterPath = Join-Path $OutputFolder "DORA-Evidence-MASTER.csv"
    $sorted | Export-Csv -Path $masterPath -NoTypeInformation -Encoding UTF8

    Write-Host ""
    Write-Host "Master report: $masterPath" -ForegroundColor Green
    Write-Host "Total evidence rows collected: $($allRows.Count)" -ForegroundColor Green

    # Quick roll-up: how many rows across everything look like they need attention
    $needsAttention = $allRows | Where-Object {
        $_.Status -match "Attention needed|NO EVIDENCE|Not confirmed|Attention" -or
        $_.Status -match "^\d+ / \d+" # e.g. "3 / 40 resource(s)"
    }
    Write-Host ""
    Write-Host "Rows flagged 'Attention needed' or similar across all scripts: $($needsAttention.Count)" -ForegroundColor Yellow
    Write-Host "(This is a rough text-match count for orientation only — read the actual" -ForegroundColor Yellow
    Write-Host " Status/Evidence/SuggestedNote columns in the master CSV, don't rely on this number alone.)" -ForegroundColor Yellow

    Write-Host ""
    Write-Host "Breakdown by DORA Article:" -ForegroundColor Cyan
    $allRows | Group-Object Article | Sort-Object { [int]$_.Name } | ForEach-Object {
        Write-Host "  Article $($_.Name): $($_.Count) finding(s)"
    }
}

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run log
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
Write-Host ""
Write-Host "======================================================================" -ForegroundColor Magenta
Write-Host " Run summary" -ForegroundColor Magenta
Write-Host "======================================================================" -ForegroundColor Magenta
$runLog | Format-Table -AutoSize

$runLogPath = Join-Path $OutputFolder "run-log.csv"
$runLog | Export-Csv -Path $runLogPath -NoTypeInformation -Encoding UTF8
Write-Host "Run log written to: $runLogPath" -ForegroundColor Green

Write-Host ""
Write-Host "REMINDER: every row in the master CSV is evidence, not a compliance answer." -ForegroundColor Red
Write-Host "Use the Article/Section columns to find the matching question in the DORA" -ForegroundColor Red
Write-Host "Self-Assessment workbook, and use the Evidence/SuggestedNote columns to" -ForegroundColor Red
Write-Host "inform — not replace — the human judgment call on Yes/Partly/No." -ForegroundColor Red
